# promise: #822
# The sidebar's + menu takes the space's palette for the Mac's appearance, as Arc 1.174.2 does (measured 26 Nov 2026 on a
# light space in both modes): light with black titles in Light mode, dark with white titles in Dark mode. Reported on a
# grey space in Light mode, where Cra drew it dark. View ▸ Appearance stands in for the Mac's setting here.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=1
wait 2
cra://action/appearanceLight
wait 1
cra://debug?plusMenu=light
expect-log plus menu light: fill=#F[0-9A-F]{5} ink=#000000 disabled=#ABABAB dark=0
cra://action/appearanceDark
wait 1
cra://debug?plusMenu=dark
expect-log plus menu dark: fill=#[0-2][0-9A-F]{5} ink=#FFFFFF disabled=#797881 dark=1
cra://action/appearanceAutomatic
